{"id":32779,"name":"Behavioral Economics and Psychology (BA)","kind":"major","degree":"BA","catalog":"2026-2027\nUSC Catalogue","source":"https://catalogue.usc.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=22&poid=32779","intro":"The Behavioral Economics and Psychology (BEEP) program aims to train students in a comprehensive set of skills necessary to understand how economic actors make decisions in real-life settings, to understand how these decisions affect economic and social outcomes and to design interventions to improve these outcomes. Concretely, students will:","totalUnits":null,"groups":[{"section":"","sub":"","rule":"","courses":[],"notes":["acquire knowledge about human cognition and decision-making and become capable of modeling behavior;","study how individual behavior affects outcomes in strategic interactions and markets; and","learn tools to collect and analyze information relevant to the areas of inquiry explored in the program."]},{"section":"I. Foundational Theory","sub":"","rule":"","courses":[{"code":"ECON 203g","title":"Principles of Microeconomics","units":"4","or":false},{"code":"ECON 303","title":"Intermediate Microeconomic Theory","units":"4","or":false},{"code":"PSYC 100Lg","title":"Introduction to Psychology","units":"4","or":false}],"notes":[]},{"section":"II. Techniques and Methods","sub":"","rule":"","courses":[{"code":"ECON 317","title":"Introduction to Statistics for Economists","units":"4","or":false},{"code":"TAC 115","title":"Programming in Python","units":"2","or":true},{"code":"TAC 116","title":"Accelerated Programming in Python","units":"2","or":false},{"code":"MATH 125g","title":"Calculus I","units":"4","or":false},{"code":"PSYC 314L","title":"Experimental Research Methods","units":"4","or":false},{"code":"PSYC 316L","title":"Non-Experimental Research Methods","units":"4","or":false}],"notes":[]},{"section":"III. Electives","sub":"","rule":"","courses":[{"code":"ECON 318","title":"Introduction to Econometrics","units":"4","or":false},{"code"